  "falsification_arm": {
    "design": "10% of test rows have their labels replaced with pure noise; a working uncertainty gate must route these to review more often than clean rows",
    "alpha_used": 0.01,
    "conformal_gate": {
      "review_rate_corrupted": 0.8401,
      "review_rate_clean": 0.8445,
      "lift": -0.0044
    },
    "distance_baseline": {
      "review_rate_corrupted": 0.8326,
      "review_rate_clean": 0.8453,
      "lift": -0.0128
    },
    "gate_can_fire": false,
    "note": "label corruption is invisible to any gate that sees only x and p(x) \u2014 neither policy observes the label. A near-zero lift for BOTH is therefore the expected and correct result, and it says something important: predictive uncertainty from this model cannot detect label noise, so 'route the uncertain cases' does not mean 'route the cases the model gets wrong'."
  },
